title: loop2_research_wing_on_enter
---
<<if not $loop2_opened>>
    <<jump loop2_opening>>
<<elseif not $loop2_split_seen>>
    <<jump loop2_split>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_opening
---
Narrator: You come to on the floor. Ears ringing. Emergency lighting. Again.
Narrator: The bulkhead door is being cut through. The same door. The same sound.
Orin: On your feet.
Doss: Cover left.
Kaleo: Optimal engagement zones remain unchanged from —
Kaleo: I am calculating optimal engagement zones.
<<set $loop2_opened = true>>
===

title: loop2_split
---
Orin: Stay with me. I know what has to be done.
Doss: You want to survive this? Stick with me. I've been in worse.
Kaleo: I should note that statistically, your survival odds are highest if —
Narrator: \[Kaleo's terminal cuts out.\]
-> \[Follow Orin.\]
    <<set $companion = "orin">>
    <<set $companion_orin = true>>
    <<set $loop2_split_seen = true>>
    <<jump loop2_post_split_orin>>
-> \[Follow Doss.\]
    <<set $companion = "doss">>
    <<set $companion_doss = true>>
    <<set $loop2_split_seen = true>>
    <<jump loop2_post_split_doss>>
===

title: loop2_research_wing_on_interact
---
<<if not $constancy_literature_found>>
    <<jump loop2_constancy_literature>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_constancy_literature
---
Narrator: A pamphlet, dropped during the breach. Dense text, no faction markings. The title: 'ON THE GIVEN SHAPE OF THINGS.'
Narrator: The argument inside is not what you expected. It is not religious in the way you assumed. It is worked-out. Careful. Angry in a way that has had time to become precise.
Narrator: The core claim: every act of temporal manipulation creates a wound in causality that cannot be healed, only accumulated. The loop you are living in is, according to this document, exactly what they predicted.
<<set $constancy_literature_found = true>>
===

title: loop2_command_deck_on_enter
---
<<if $companion == "orin" and $companion_orin and not $loop2_post_split_orin_seen>>
    <<jump loop2_post_split_orin>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_post_split_orin
---
Orin: The mission is the same. Contain the anomaly. Everything else is secondary.
<<set $loop2_post_split_orin_seen = true>>
-> Have we done this before?
    <<jump loop2_orin_deflect_loop>>
-> \[Follow her lead.\]
===

title: loop2_orin_deflect_loop
---
Orin: That's not a useful question right now.
Narrator: She doesn't look at you when she says it.
===

title: loop2_command_deck_on_interact
---
<<if $companion == "orin" and $companion_orin and not $orin_locket_noticed>>
    <<jump loop2_orin_locket>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_orin_locket
---
Narrator: The locket she's wearing — you've seen it before. But it's different. The clasp. The worn edge on the left side instead of the right.
<<set $orin_locket_noticed = true>>
-> Your locket — it's different from before.
    <<jump loop2_orin_locket_press>>
-> \[Say nothing.\]
===

title: loop2_orin_locket_press
---
Orin: Before from when?
Narrator: A beat too long. A careful answer to an impossible question.
===

title: loop2_military_annex_on_enter
---
<<if $companion == "doss" and $companion_doss and not $loop2_post_split_doss_seen>>
    <<jump loop2_post_split_doss>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_post_split_doss
---
Doss: Same as before. Armory, then the anomaly chamber.
Narrator: Same as before. He said it like it meant nothing.
<<set $loop2_post_split_doss_seen = true>>
-> Same as before?
    <<jump loop2_doss_slip_caught>>
-> \[Follow him.\]
===

title: loop2_doss_slip_caught
---
Doss: Standard protocol. Same as any breach situation.
Narrator: He doesn't break stride.
===

title: loop2_military_annex_on_interact
---
<<if not $doss_armor_noticed>>
    <<jump loop2_doss_armor>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_doss_armor
---
Narrator: Doss's armor, on close inspection, isn't station-issue. The seams are wrong. The make is different — older, heavier, with repair patches on the shoulder that don't match any fabricator on the manifest.
Narrator: It's battlefield salvage. From somewhere.
<<set $doss_armor_noticed = true>>
-> Where did you get that armor?
    <<jump loop2_doss_armor_question>>
-> \[Note it and move on.\]
===

title: loop2_doss_armor_question
---
Doss: Old kit. I'm used to it.
Narrator: He doesn't ask why you're asking.
===

title: loop2_research_wing_salvage_operative_on_interact
---
<<if not $rw_salvage_op_loop2_seen>>
    <<jump loop2_rw_salvage_op>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_rw_salvage_op
---
Narrator: She's in the same spot. The same kit bag. She looks at you the way people look at someone they've met before but can't place.
SalvageOperative: You again. Thought you'd be further along by now.
Narrator: She couldn't know that.
<<set $rw_salvage_op_loop2_seen = true>>
-> Have we met before?
    <<jump loop2_rw_salvage_op_deja_vu>>
-> What's the situation?
    <<jump loop2_rw_salvage_op_situation>>
===

title: loop2_rw_salvage_op_deja_vu
---
SalvageOperative: I don't think so.
Narrator: A pause that goes a beat too long.
SalvageOperative: Must be a type. Researchers all look the same in emergency lighting.
===

title: loop2_rw_salvage_op_situation
---
SalvageOperative: Worse than before. Scavengers are deeper in than they should be this fast. Something is letting them through.
SalvageOperative: And the readings from the Anomaly Chamber — they were bad last time I checked. They're worse now.
Narrator: Last time.
===

title: loop2_docking_bay_gun_for_hire_on_interact
---
<<if not $gfh_docking_loop2_seen>>
    <<jump loop2_gfh>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_gfh
---
GunForHire: You made it. I had even odds on that.
Narrator: Not sarcasm. A genuine assessment.
GunForHire: Situation's shifted. Raiders showed up through the port — not the same crowd as last —
Narrator: He stops.
GunForHire: Not the same crowd as what I was expecting. They're organised.
<<set $gfh_docking_loop2_seen = true>>
-> Last time?
    <<jump loop2_gfh_slip>>
-> What do the Raiders want?
    <<jump loop2_gfh_raiders>>
===

title: loop2_gfh_slip
---
GunForHire: Figure of speech.
Narrator: His eyes don't agree.
===

title: loop2_gfh_raiders
---
GunForHire: Salvage. Same as always. But they're taking more risks than the payout justifies. Something's drawing them in.
GunForHire: My advice: don't give them a reason to focus on you specifically.
===

title: loop2_medical_bay_salvage_operative_on_interact
---
<<if not $med_salvage_op_loop2_seen>>
    <<jump loop2_med_salvage_op>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_med_salvage_op
---
SalvageOperative: Back again.
Narrator: She doesn't mean anything by it. Or she does and doesn't know why.
SalvageOperative: I've got supplies. Take what you need — I'm starting to think holding inventory is less useful than moving it.
<<set $med_salvage_op_loop2_seen = true>>
-> Are you planning to leave?
    <<jump loop2_med_salvage_op_leaving>>
-> \[Take the supplies.\]
===

title: loop2_med_salvage_op_leaving
---
SalvageOperative: Thinking about it. Something about this place —
Narrator: She doesn't finish the sentence.
SalvageOperative: The readings are wrong. Have been since before the breach. I've been telling myself it's equipment error.
===

title: loop2_medical_bay_station_guard_on_interact
---
<<if not $med_guard_loop2_seen>>
    <<jump loop2_med_guard>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_med_guard
---
StationGuard: Researcher. Glad you're still moving.
Narrator: Something in her posture is tighter than it was. Not hostile — strained.
StationGuard: The temporal readings near the Surgery are wrong. Instruments are disagreeing with themselves.
<<set $med_guard_loop2_seen = true>>
-> What do you mean, disagreeing?
    <<jump loop2_med_guard_readings>>
-> Are you all right?
    <<jump loop2_med_guard_wellbeing>>
===

title: loop2_med_guard_readings
---
StationGuard: Two sensors in the same room giving different timestamps for the same event. By six seconds. That shouldn't be possible.
StationGuard: I logged it. Orin's team said it was a calibration error. But the gap is getting wider each time I check.
===

title: loop2_med_guard_wellbeing
---
StationGuard: I'm fine. Just — have you noticed anything strange about your memory? Like you're filling in gaps you shouldn't have?
Narrator: She asks it carefully. Like she's been wondering whether to ask for a while.
===

title: loop2_systems_core_on_enter
---
<<if not $loop2_kaleo_terminal_seen>>
    <<jump loop2_kaleo_terminal>>
<<endif>>
===

title: loop2_kaleo_terminal
---
Narrator: A terminal near the corridor displays a status readout that wasn't there before. UNIT KALEO — OPERATIONAL. MONITORING.
Narrator: It isn't a system error. The display is deliberate. Something is watching your progress through the station.
<<set $loop2_kaleo_terminal_seen = true>>
===
